WEBVTT

00:10.480 --> 00:11.190
JUJUTSU KAISEN

00:34.470 --> 00:38.680
JUJUTSU KAISEN
The Culling Game Part 1

01:29.990 --> 01:32.740
In Japan, 99.9% of Criminal Trials End in a Guilty Verdict

01:42.380 --> 01:44.270
I owned a cat.

01:45.760 --> 01:46.830
Continue.

01:47.890 --> 01:50.600
A cop suddenly started speaking to me.

01:51.050 --> 01:53.250
Then there were two, then three of them.

01:53.660 --> 01:55.330
I thought, "If they take me in now,

01:55.330 --> 01:56.830
my cat is going to die."

01:57.350 --> 01:59.150
My place doesn't allow us to own them.

01:59.600 --> 02:02.470
So I was the only one who knew about it.

02:03.220 --> 02:05.270
In Morioka City, Iwate Prefecture,

02:05.270 --> 02:07.230
in March of 2016,

02:07.640 --> 02:09.610
two people—
a young girl and her mother—

02:09.610 --> 02:13.050
were found fatally stabbed
in their own home.

02:14.520 --> 02:15.990
The Morioka Prosecutor's Office

02:15.990 --> 02:18.130
indicted Keita Oe, who lived nearby,

02:18.130 --> 02:21.290
on charges of felony murder and robbery.

02:21.740 --> 02:23.810
The events leading to
his arrest were thus:

02:24.330 --> 02:28.540
Oe fled during police questioning
by officers on patrol,

02:28.090 --> 02:29.250
Hey! Stop!

02:28.540 --> 02:30.460
and after police chased
him into his home,

02:30.930 --> 02:35.010
the officers who chased him discovered
a blade with blood on it,

02:36.400 --> 02:37.970
and then arrested him
in flagrante delicto.

02:39.700 --> 02:41.840
Later DNA analysis

02:39.760 --> 02:41.040
There he is!

02:41.040 --> 02:41.840
Come on, behave!

02:41.840 --> 02:45.310
revealed the blood on the blade
matched the victims' DNA.

02:44.190 --> 02:45.310
Stop struggling!

02:46.690 --> 02:49.630
Oe consistently denied all
culpability for the crime.

02:49.630 --> 02:52.080
On the blade collected
as evidence, he insisted...

02:52.080 --> 02:53.420
I just picked it up.

02:53.770 --> 02:54.780
It wasn't mine.

02:55.590 --> 02:57.910
That's a bit hard to believe, isn't it?

02:57.910 --> 03:01.830
I mean, he refused the questioning
because he felt guilty, right?

03:02.340 --> 03:05.510
No. He was previously a victim
of wrongful questioning

03:05.510 --> 03:09.380
because an acquaintance of his
was using drugs in the past.

03:09.380 --> 03:11.890
You're saying that traumatized him?

03:11.890 --> 03:14.260
Even so, "I picked it up"?

03:14.260 --> 03:17.440
A bloody kitchen knife? Why?

03:17.890 --> 03:21.100
He claims he was planning to
turn it in to the police later.

03:21.100 --> 03:22.320
"Later"?!

03:23.330 --> 03:24.710
I know.

03:24.710 --> 03:26.310
His claims are all hard to believe.

03:26.960 --> 03:29.320
But when you consider Oe's background—

03:29.320 --> 03:33.300
the fact that he works as a live-in
employee at a non-profit organization—

03:33.300 --> 03:35.530
it starts sounding plausible.

03:35.940 --> 03:37.780
A non-profit?

03:38.740 --> 03:40.900
They work with the elderly
who have no place to go,

03:40.900 --> 03:44.430
primarily running a shelter and providing
support for their independent living.

03:44.430 --> 03:47.910
Oe's job was taking care
of the elderly there.

03:48.330 --> 03:51.160
However, they didn't pay him a wage.

03:51.630 --> 03:54.590
They only supplied him with goods
like groceries, boxed lunches,

03:54.590 --> 03:57.350
and the occasional New Year's
gift of pocket money.

03:57.680 --> 03:59.410
Yet despite that,

03:59.410 --> 04:02.850
they collected 50,000 yen
a month from him as rent.

04:02.850 --> 04:03.950
Brutal.

04:04.370 --> 04:07.940
Apparently, quite a few of the
residents have prior records.

04:07.940 --> 04:11.640
Furthermore, the reason he was delayed in
turning over the weapon he found was...

04:11.960 --> 04:15.650
The rules say we can't call
any cop cars or ambulances.

04:15.950 --> 04:18.010
Because they'd bother the neighbors.

04:19.900 --> 04:34.420
Higuruma Law Office

04:19.900 --> 04:23.060
That organization sounds
kinda shady, doesn't it?

04:23.060 --> 04:23.960
Yeah.

04:23.960 --> 04:26.370
It's extremely close to
being outright illegal.

04:26.850 --> 04:30.740
We've already seen an increase
in suspiciously managed NPOs

04:30.740 --> 04:33.920
since the earthquake relief funds
started flowing into this region.

04:34.420 --> 04:37.270
So it's not surprising the murder
weapon was just lying around.

04:37.980 --> 04:41.420
There's a good possibility Oe's innocent.

04:43.060 --> 04:46.470
First, we'll investigate the
organization's activities and tax filings,

04:46.470 --> 04:49.350
then run background checks
on all the residents.

04:49.350 --> 04:52.280
I'll focus on getting
information out of Oe.

04:52.280 --> 04:54.070
You handle the investigation, Shimizu.

04:54.070 --> 04:57.570
You're dumping a huge job like
that on me out of the blue?

04:59.420 --> 05:01.080
Could you take care of his cat, too?

05:01.080 --> 05:02.160
The cat?!

05:03.110 --> 05:06.780
The commission for public defense cases
is low, despite how much work they take.

05:07.110 --> 05:09.360
The public assumes he's guilty, too.

05:09.360 --> 05:12.120
Plus, there's no suspended
sentence in murder cases,

05:12.120 --> 05:13.800
and he could receive the death penalty.

05:13.800 --> 05:15.750
There's nothing to gain here.

05:16.910 --> 05:21.970
Jeez, Higuruma-san! Why did you
go and accept a case like this?

05:21.970 --> 05:23.430
It's fine every now and then.

05:23.890 --> 05:26.540
If we stuck to easy work,
our skills would dull.

05:26.810 --> 05:28.700
It's more than every now and then!

05:29.020 --> 05:30.860
It's more than every now and then!

05:31.370 --> 05:33.770
You're saying your thoughts out loud.

05:35.980 --> 05:38.970
Sounds like Higuruma-kun
hasn't changed then.

05:39.540 --> 05:42.860
It's rough when an independent
lawyer isn't in it for the money.

05:43.320 --> 05:48.620
At least it's not so bad that I'm being
told to run a café on the side like you.

05:48.620 --> 05:50.500
But when you say he hasn't changed,

05:50.500 --> 05:52.910
you mean Higuruma-san's
always been like this?

05:52.910 --> 05:54.660
Hm? No.

05:55.130 --> 05:57.770
I think he actually used to be worse.

05:57.770 --> 05:58.670
Huh?

05:59.360 --> 06:01.390
Back when he was with us,

06:01.390 --> 06:04.510
he was in charge of a case of
reckless driving resulting in injury.

06:04.510 --> 06:06.360
Oh, a drunk driving one.

06:07.260 --> 06:09.620
The defendant was nineteen,

06:09.620 --> 06:14.320
and his coworkers had coerced him into
both the drinking and the driving.

06:14.320 --> 06:17.220
However, those involved all
aligned their stories,

06:17.220 --> 06:19.150
and he wasn't able to prepare
money for a settlement,

06:19.150 --> 06:21.640
nor were we able to get
him a suspended sentence.

06:27.340 --> 06:28.640
Liar!

06:30.370 --> 06:33.120
You said they'd find me innocent!

06:33.830 --> 06:37.840
You told him you'd manage to get
a suspended sentence, though,

06:37.840 --> 06:40.320
not an innocent verdict.

06:40.990 --> 06:42.740
Have you learned your lesson now?

06:42.740 --> 06:45.980
Quit being a criminal defense
lawyer for impossible cases.

06:46.560 --> 06:50.600
Trying to save the weak
may be a noble endeavor,

06:50.990 --> 06:53.550
but there's a limit to what
lawyers like us can do

06:53.550 --> 06:56.080
without understanding from
the courts and prosecutors.

06:55.260 --> 06:57.290
Oh, I want to ride that!

06:56.530 --> 07:00.020
It's not worth continuing when
your clients resent you.

07:01.780 --> 07:05.980
They're at the end of their rope,
both mentally and financially.

07:06.390 --> 07:08.690
I can't blame them for lashing out at me.

07:11.020 --> 07:14.490
But what about your mental
state, Higuruma-kun?

07:15.580 --> 07:16.610
I...

07:38.750 --> 07:41.500
We find the defendant...

07:41.940 --> 07:43.200
innocent.

07:48.610 --> 07:50.520
We actually won this case?

07:52.410 --> 07:53.650
Not yet.

07:55.170 --> 07:57.020
They'll appeal right away.

07:57.410 --> 07:58.900
The Morioka Mother-Child Murder Incident
Questionable Innocent Verdict.
"It Was Bought"
Former Judge Comments on Crooked Lawyer's Statements

08:00.710 --> 08:02.420
The verdict was innocent.
Guess even murderers go free
if they can pay up.
How much did he dump on this...
The law is dead. Prosecutors are useless.

08:02.420 --> 08:04.170
Refusing to Accept the Current Ruling,
They Have Appealed Seeking A Revision

08:02.420 --> 08:04.170
Morioka Prosecutor's Office

08:02.640 --> 08:04.170
The prosecution has...

08:13.300 --> 08:17.800
Nothing stolen was found
in Oe-san's room.

08:17.800 --> 08:22.770
There was another person in the same NPO
who went missing right after the crime.

08:23.100 --> 08:26.570
The fact that you were caught on a
convenience store's security camera feed

08:26.570 --> 08:30.920
during the time of the crime determined
from the corpse played a major role, too.

08:31.350 --> 08:34.410
Good thing you don't cook
for yourself, Oe-san!

08:34.910 --> 08:36.310
Counselor Higuruma...

08:36.700 --> 08:38.460
Thank you so much.

08:38.990 --> 08:41.430
No need for "Counselor."

08:41.430 --> 08:44.570
Besides, we're not in the clear yet.
We still have the second trial.

08:45.010 --> 08:46.210
I worked hard, too.

08:45.790 --> 08:47.210
That's not what I mean.

08:50.000 --> 08:53.170
Thank you for believing me!

08:56.560 --> 08:59.060
Appeal Trial (Second Trial)

08:59.060 --> 09:02.060
Guilty. Life Sentence.

09:02.370 --> 09:07.200
While defense lawyers have to work
with limited budgets and manpower,

09:07.200 --> 09:11.310
prosecutors can pour manpower and
taxpayer money into digging up evidence.

09:11.310 --> 09:13.680
That's fine. That's how the system works.

09:14.020 --> 09:15.070
However,

09:15.330 --> 09:19.270
the prosecutors didn't submit any new
evidence during the second trial.

09:21.270 --> 09:24.960
The judge recognized
their absurd claim that

09:24.960 --> 09:27.510
"there's no reason to suspect the
missing person of the crime,"

09:27.510 --> 09:29.460
and they overturned the verdict.

09:31.370 --> 09:34.470
The highest court is always the
bottleneck for a third trial.

09:34.470 --> 09:37.060
Most final appeals are
turned away at the door.

09:37.060 --> 09:39.990
It's challenging to even
get a proper trial there.

09:40.850 --> 09:44.370
This trial was destined for a
guilty verdict from the start.

09:51.670 --> 09:53.030
Why are you

09:55.100 --> 09:56.690
looking at me that way?

09:59.480 --> 10:03.620
But what about your mental
state, Higuruma-kun?

10:05.500 --> 10:08.980
I'm not trying to tout the
ideal of saving the weak.

10:09.800 --> 10:12.140
It's just always gone against my nature

10:12.140 --> 10:14.430
to leave things alone when
I feel like they're wrong.

10:15.040 --> 10:17.580
I've just never managed
to fix that habit.

10:18.360 --> 10:22.750
The goddess of justice blinds her sight
to maintain fairness under the law,

10:22.750 --> 10:26.560
and people turn a blind eye to all
kinds of things to protect themselves.

10:26.970 --> 10:31.260
But I don't want to brush away the
hands clinging to me for help,

10:35.120 --> 10:37.730
so I want to keep my eyes open, at least.

10:42.060 --> 10:44.760
If there are any objections
to today's trial,

10:44.760 --> 10:49.630
submit your final appeal in writing
within fifteen days, including today.

11:01.180 --> 11:02.890
Higuruma-san?

11:06.240 --> 11:08.310
Everyone come back.

11:13.260 --> 11:15.090
We're having a retrial.

11:15.570 --> 11:16.520
Culling Game Player

11:16.520 --> 11:19.280
Hiromi Higuruma

11:19.280 --> 11:20.540
Higuruma is in...

11:20.540 --> 11:21.620
...Shinjuku.

11:21.620 --> 11:22.410
...Ikebukuro.

11:22.410 --> 11:23.030
Got it?

11:23.360 --> 11:24.490
Shinjuku?

11:24.890 --> 11:27.090
I hope Itadori is heading there, too.

11:27.090 --> 11:28.610
Ikebukuro, huh?

11:28.610 --> 11:30.330
I wonder if Fushiguro's there, too.

11:34.370 --> 11:36.910
Isn't she a little late?

11:36.910 --> 11:39.340
When is that girl

11:39.340 --> 11:43.260
going to bring me my next sucker?

11:44.010 --> 11:47.010
Episode 55
Tokyo No. 1 Colony, Part 2

11:50.550 --> 11:53.150
Huh? Wh-What?

11:53.150 --> 11:55.240
Oh, no, no.

11:55.240 --> 11:56.860
Not like that at all.

11:56.860 --> 11:59.470
Hey, what are you doing?

11:59.870 --> 12:01.370
Like this! This!

12:01.370 --> 12:03.120
R-Right.

12:03.120 --> 12:04.860
Why are you keeping quiet?

12:05.130 --> 12:07.620
You're better off laughing!

12:08.610 --> 12:10.460
Come on, come on!

12:11.060 --> 12:13.430
Oh, dear. What did I tell you?

12:12.150 --> 12:13.350
What's your problem?

12:13.350 --> 12:13.990
What's your problem?!

12:14.000 --> 12:15.710
Not that I actually told you.

12:14.470 --> 12:15.630
There you go.

12:16.250 --> 12:18.070
But why can't you understand?

12:16.890 --> 12:18.280
What's your problem?!

12:18.070 --> 12:19.550
Are you an idiot?!

12:18.540 --> 12:19.980
What's your problem?!

12:19.550 --> 12:22.750
These guys aren't that smart or athletic,

12:22.750 --> 12:25.340
but they're brimming with pride.

12:25.340 --> 12:29.850
You just have to match their vibe and
joke around so you don't hurt that pride.

12:30.490 --> 12:34.100
Then you won't get targeted
by anyone else, either.

12:34.100 --> 12:36.550
And you can occasionally
enjoy a good time, too.

12:37.480 --> 12:38.760
Stop it.

12:42.020 --> 12:43.980
Here comes another idiot.

12:43.980 --> 12:46.320
Is that uniform from West Middle?

12:46.320 --> 12:48.070
You're a middle schooler?

12:48.070 --> 12:50.580
You weren't showing respect, were you?

12:50.580 --> 12:53.450
So you need to

12:53.450 --> 12:54.660
learn a lesson!

12:55.400 --> 12:56.250
Huh?

13:01.700 --> 13:02.700
Huh?

13:10.290 --> 13:12.550
No violence!

13:16.970 --> 13:18.520
Come here!

13:29.250 --> 13:30.300
What about you?

13:30.610 --> 13:31.610
Culling Game Player

13:33.740 --> 13:35.740
M-Me?

13:35.740 --> 13:37.750
Yuji Itadori
Rin Amai

13:36.810 --> 13:37.750
Hey.

13:37.750 --> 13:39.100
What?

13:39.100 --> 13:42.320
You aren't planning to go through
Ikebukuro to reach Shinjuku, are you?

13:42.880 --> 13:44.740
That area's rich with supplies.

13:45.230 --> 13:47.640
We're more likely to
encounter other Players.

13:47.900 --> 13:50.630
There are two reasons for going this way.

13:50.630 --> 13:52.550
The route is easy to follow,

13:52.550 --> 13:54.790
and I have a base nearby.

13:56.340 --> 13:58.690
At least let me take a shower.

13:58.690 --> 14:01.340
I haven't gotten much
rest since yesterday.

14:04.340 --> 14:07.400
Higuruma uses this theater as his base.

14:07.400 --> 14:09.450
Assuming he hasn't moved, that is.

14:09.450 --> 14:10.710
Cool!

14:10.710 --> 14:13.020
You've been a big help! Thanks!

14:13.550 --> 14:16.130
Oh, h-h-hold on!

14:16.450 --> 14:17.490
What?

14:17.850 --> 14:19.650
Are you seriously going?

14:19.650 --> 14:23.460
I'd rather reunite with my friend
first, but we're in a hurry.

14:23.790 --> 14:26.510
I haven't met Higuruma myself,

14:26.510 --> 14:29.970
but he once beat Haba-san to a pulp.

14:29.970 --> 14:31.590
Then I'll be fine!

14:31.590 --> 14:35.270
I beat that propeller head, too,
so I'll at least be able to run away.

14:35.970 --> 14:37.220
Maybe so

14:36.840 --> 14:37.960
See you later!

14:39.730 --> 14:40.950
Say it!

14:42.220 --> 14:43.760
Say it, man!

14:44.680 --> 14:46.760
You should stop doing this!

14:52.520 --> 14:53.690
I'm sorry,

14:54.880 --> 14:56.120
Itadori.

14:58.970 --> 15:02.460
Higuruma? Oh...

15:02.460 --> 15:06.130
Sorry, but I'm Reggie.

15:06.130 --> 15:09.190
She deceived you.

15:12.710 --> 15:14.480
Don't give me that look.

15:14.480 --> 15:16.780
I'm not frightened at all.

15:16.780 --> 15:18.430
Just so you know, Reggie—

15:18.430 --> 15:19.230
Stop talking.

15:23.180 --> 15:24.370
Oho?

15:25.960 --> 15:27.820
We're wasting time.

15:38.710 --> 15:39.740
Who's there?

15:40.190 --> 15:42.240
What are you doing over there?

15:44.130 --> 15:45.360
I could ask you that.

15:48.120 --> 15:51.900
Have you ever taken a bath
while in your clothes?

15:51.900 --> 15:53.010
Never.

15:53.820 --> 15:56.940
It feels better than I expected.

15:59.520 --> 16:00.630
Right.

16:02.550 --> 16:04.540
Back when I was in elementary school,

16:04.540 --> 16:07.580
I loved our classes on
swimming in clothes.

16:08.230 --> 16:11.830
So many things have stopped
mattering lately,

16:11.830 --> 16:16.440
so I've been challenging myself to
try things I assumed I shouldn't do.

16:16.440 --> 16:19.990
I've basically gone off the
rails after hitting my mid-30s.

16:19.990 --> 16:21.040
Is that funny?

16:21.590 --> 16:23.530
It's kind of amusing.

16:24.050 --> 16:25.870
You're Higuruma, right?

16:26.350 --> 16:27.820
In the flesh.

16:27.820 --> 16:28.960
I want to talk.

16:29.780 --> 16:31.930
Hold on. Wait, wait.

16:32.260 --> 16:34.060
I'm a lawyer.

16:34.060 --> 16:38.670
Talking to me will incur a consultation
fee of 5,000 yen every half hour.

16:38.670 --> 16:39.520
Huh?!

16:41.360 --> 16:42.810
I'm kidding.

16:42.810 --> 16:45.820
I just wanted to try acting
like a nasty lawyer for once.

16:46.860 --> 16:48.350
I see.

16:48.890 --> 16:50.930
What's this guy doing?

16:51.550 --> 16:53.520
You have 100 points, right?

16:54.190 --> 16:56.620
He's not a past sorcerer
who's been incarnated.

16:56.870 --> 16:59.900
He's a modern sorcerer whose
technique was activated!

16:59.900 --> 17:01.410
We can talk it out!

17:01.410 --> 17:02.940
There's room for negotiation!

17:03.360 --> 17:05.610
Oh, yeah. You pass.

17:05.960 --> 17:06.750
Huh?

17:06.750 --> 17:09.010
That's enough. I can tell now.

17:09.010 --> 17:10.960
That's quite the shikigami.

17:10.960 --> 17:12.520
You're strong, right?

17:12.520 --> 17:16.310
If you were weak, I'd just
kill you as another mark.

17:16.310 --> 17:17.520
But you're good.

17:17.520 --> 17:18.890
Let's work together.

17:18.890 --> 17:20.240
What gives?!

17:20.240 --> 17:21.830
I never heard about this!

17:22.960 --> 17:24.810
What are you getting at?

17:24.810 --> 17:28.470
How much do you know
about this Culling Game?

17:29.170 --> 17:30.450
It's a ritual, right?

17:30.970 --> 17:34.220
It uses the cursed energy of
the Players inside the barriers

17:34.220 --> 17:36.790
to ferry the people of
Japan to the other side

17:36.790 --> 17:39.080
and change them into something inhuman.

17:39.710 --> 17:42.170
Guess I should stay quiet
about Tengen-sama.

17:42.170 --> 17:45.810
Oh? Do you know Kenjaku, then?

17:46.870 --> 17:48.670
I knew there'd be one!

17:49.130 --> 17:51.650
A sorcerer connected to Kenjaku!

17:52.480 --> 17:54.780
Uh, so, to be frank,

17:55.590 --> 17:59.000
we want to stop the Culling Game.

17:59.770 --> 18:01.050
Er, time out.

18:01.050 --> 18:04.550
When I say "stop it," I mean we want
to negate the compulsory killing.

18:04.950 --> 18:08.790
Please let us use your 100 points
to add a rule toward that end.

18:09.310 --> 18:11.440
Allow me to be frank, as well.

18:12.010 --> 18:13.080
I refuse.

18:14.760 --> 18:16.290
Is that another joke?

18:17.100 --> 18:18.170
No.

18:18.170 --> 18:21.700
I just sense potential
in the Culling Game.

18:21.700 --> 18:24.160
Complete Book of the Six Codes

18:22.130 --> 18:24.160
Sometimes the law is powerless.

18:24.160 --> 18:27.620
But what about the rules
of this Culling Game?

18:27.620 --> 18:30.210
If the power I've been granted is real,

18:30.210 --> 18:32.090
then those rules must be, too.

18:32.090 --> 18:36.460
What you just said about Players'
cursed energy being used?

18:36.460 --> 18:38.290
That's probably a bluff.

18:38.290 --> 18:39.100
What?

18:39.100 --> 18:44.280
Well, less of a bluff,
and more Plan B or C.

18:44.280 --> 18:46.060
I have three reasons.

18:46.560 --> 18:48.250
The number of Players.

18:48.250 --> 18:50.150
The strength gap between Players.

18:50.150 --> 18:51.850
The barriers' rules.

18:52.290 --> 18:57.320
If roughly 1,000 people were equally
split up between the ten Colonies,

18:57.320 --> 18:59.850
that would be 100 per Colony.

18:59.850 --> 19:03.130
But among the Players are sorcerers

19:03.130 --> 19:05.160
like Kashimo or Higuruma,

19:05.160 --> 19:06.810
who are much stronger than the rest.

19:06.810 --> 19:10.770
These two alone have already
culled sixty sorcerers.

19:10.770 --> 19:14.370
There's probably one like
them in each Colony.

19:14.790 --> 19:17.610
So the weak are weeded out early on,

19:17.610 --> 19:19.990
and the Culling Game
will reach a stalemate?

19:20.670 --> 19:22.630
I certainly did sense that.

19:22.990 --> 19:25.290
The Colony has been too quiet.

19:25.290 --> 19:26.890
It already has.

19:26.890 --> 19:29.930
At least here in Tokyo No. 1.

19:29.930 --> 19:33.820
On top of that, there's the teleportation
when people enter the Colony.

19:33.820 --> 19:36.070
It serves to spread them out,

19:36.070 --> 19:38.140
but its main goal is likely to encourage

19:38.140 --> 19:40.610
an early second awakening
of modern sorcerers.

19:40.610 --> 19:43.330
There are some who die during
the teleportation, too.

19:43.330 --> 19:46.240
If he was really trying to use
the Players' cursed energy,

19:46.240 --> 19:48.870
he would want the greatest
number of sorcerers

19:48.870 --> 19:51.580
to fight for the longest time possible.

19:51.580 --> 19:56.330
What if people who broke the
rules were punished by physics,

19:56.330 --> 20:00.330
without any need for indictments,
prosecutions, or arguments at trials?

20:00.330 --> 20:02.650
Wouldn't that be wonderful?

20:02.650 --> 20:04.940
I'll acknowledge there are
issues with the current rules,

20:04.940 --> 20:08.300
but I want to watch over the system
serving as a basis for this game.

20:08.300 --> 20:10.800
It won't do for it to end too soon.

20:10.800 --> 20:13.750
I'd especially love to witness
the stripping of a technique

20:10.810 --> 20:16.560
2: Players breaching the first rule
shall be stripped of their technique.
8:  Players who do not show a change in points
within 19 days of joining or acquiring points
shall be stripped of their technique.

20:13.750 --> 20:16.560
mentioned in Rule 2 and 8 at least once.

20:16.940 --> 20:19.870
It's better for the rules if
being stripped means death, too.

20:20.320 --> 20:23.220
The Culling Game itself is a ritual.

20:23.220 --> 20:26.300
If we take too long,
every person in this nation will die.

20:26.300 --> 20:27.650
That's a lie.

20:27.650 --> 20:30.740
The Culling Game insists
on its own permanence.

20:30.740 --> 20:33.110
I don't really get that part, either!

20:35.500 --> 20:37.180
Let me rephrase it, then.

20:37.910 --> 20:41.300
Let me use your 100 points, Higuruma!

20:42.720 --> 20:46.670
Have you ever killed someone
who ticked you off?

20:49.810 --> 20:54.160
It feels much better than I expected.

20:55.000 --> 20:56.210
A shikigami?!

20:57.360 --> 20:59.210
Higuruma has 100 points.

20:59.210 --> 21:01.640
He might have killed
twenty sorcerers already.

21:02.190 --> 21:03.870
I can't leap in recklessly.

21:04.330 --> 21:05.690
I'll go on defense,

21:05.690 --> 21:08.180
but I'll be ready to
respond to any attack!

21:10.170 --> 21:11.780
Domain Expansion.

21:12.650 --> 21:14.730
Deadly Sentencing.

21:26.900 --> 21:32.430
The rules' idea of continuation is
just a cover for the real plan.

21:32.430 --> 21:34.410
Mark my words.

21:34.410 --> 21:36.870
When only the strong remain,

21:36.870 --> 21:39.520
Kenjaku is going to drop
a bomb on the game,

21:39.520 --> 21:43.270
and the Culling Game
will fulfill its purpose.

21:54.830 --> 21:56.580
Please have a seat.

22:05.710 --> 22:07.340
Thank you for inviting me here.

23:40.730 --> 23:42.450
Now, make your argument.

23:42.450 --> 23:43.530
What happens if I'm judged guilty?

23:43.530 --> 23:44.960
Judgeman, please begin.

23:44.960 --> 23:45.890
You mean I can lie?

23:45.890 --> 23:47.610
You get one chance to make a statement.

23:47.610 --> 23:48.840
I can't control cursed energy!

23:48.840 --> 23:51.780
How can he hold his own against
me without cursed energy?

23:51.780 --> 23:53.900
I want a retrial! One more time!

23:51.990 --> 23:55.060
Next Episode
Tokyo No. 1 Colony, Part 3
